.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Handoff scratch — the cycle's working surface, deleted when the cycle ends.
#
# Both files are transient, but only one leaves a record. The plan is simply
# discarded. The findings mailbox is **promoted** at commit time into
# `docs/wiki/reviews/<date>-<slug>.md`, which is the tracked, date-keyed home
# of the dispositions behavioral rule 20 requires. Never delete a mailbox
# without promoting it first — see the `adversarial-review` skill, step 8.
#
# Note these globs match only names ending exactly in `-plan.md` / `-findings.md`;
# a suffixed variant (`auth-plan-v2.md`) is NOT ignored and will surface as
# untracked. See docs/wiki/gotchas.md § Tooling. One file per slug, no suffixes.
.claude/handoff/*-plan.md
.claude/handoff/*-findings.md
# The handoff brief (`llm-handoff` skill) is scratch too: it is a prompt for an
# external agent, not repo content, and that agent deletes it when its cycle ends.
.claude/handoff/*-handoff.md

# Obsidian per-user vault config (users open the vault themselves)
docs/.obsidian/
